 1034 "r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534805 true] [17592186311207 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534805 true] [17592186311207 1111 #uuid "a9829abb-ffba-59da-9845-aa501dc31f18" 13194139534805 true] [17592186311208 1017 #edb/ref 17592186311209 13194139534805 true] [17592186311208 1089 "q-77442" 13194139534805 true] [17592186311208 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534805 true] [17592186311208 1100 "Consider the straight line that passes through $P(4,0,-1)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨2,-6,3⟩.$ Find all the possible points $A$ on that line such that $PA=7.$" 13194139534805 true] [17592186311208 1113 #uuid "f8ced46a-f7bf-550c-ae94-d64f15be9c59" 13194139534805 true] [17592186311208 1145 "First, we find the vector equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =⟨4,0,-1⟩+t⟨2,-6,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSince $A$ lies on the line, we know that there must be a real number $t$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OA} & =⟨4,0,-1⟩+t⟨2,-6,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PA} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(⟨4,0,-1⟩+t⟨2,-6,3⟩)-⟨4,0,-1⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,⟨2,-6,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,-6t,\\,3t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $PA=7,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PA & =7 \\\\ |\\overset{\\to }{PA}| & =7 \\\\ |⟨2t,\\,-6t,\\,3t⟩| & =7 \\\\ \\sqrt{(2t)^{2}+(-6t)^{2}+(3t)^{2}} & =7 \\\\ \\sqrt{49{t}^{2}} & =7 \\\\ \\pm 7t & =7 \\\\ t & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the values $t=\\pm 1$ into the equation for the line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{1}}=⟨4,0,-1⟩+⟨2,-6,3⟩=⟨6,-6,2⟩, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{2}}=⟨4,0,-1⟩-⟨2,-6,3⟩=⟨2,6,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points are ${A}_{1}(6,-6,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(2,6,-4).$" 13194139534805 true] [17592186311209 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311210 13194139534805 true] [17592186311209 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311211 13194139534805 true] [17592186311209 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311212 13194139534805 true] [17592186311209 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311213 13194139534805 true] [17592186311209 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311214 13194139534805 true] [17592186311209 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534805 true] [17592186311209 1041 "selection" 13194139534805 true] [17592186311209 1104 #edb/ref 17592186311213 13194139534805 true] [17592186311209 1110 #uuid "1ee7d575-a0c4-5892-a256-694602bc0503" 13194139534805 true] [17592186311210 1034 "${A}_{1}(6,-6,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(10,18,8)$" 13194139534805 true] [17592186311210 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534805 true] [17592186311210 1111 #uuid "f299e4ee-0d87-5b20-b9c2-616a468cd553" 13194139534805 true] [17592186311211 1034 "${A}_{1}(10,2,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(2,6,-4)$" 13194139534805 true] [17592186311211 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534805 true] [17592186311211 1111 #uuid "9b81aa93-84f4-569d-9611-f982ef89af8b" 13194139534805 true] [17592186311212 1034 "${A}_{1}(8,-12,5)$ and ${A}_{2}(7,6,-3)$" 13194139534805 true] [17592186311212 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534805 true] [17592186311212 1111 #uuid "fc89ac3c-5852-5b09-80a0-e4ce2ddea766" 13194139534805 true] [17592186311213 1034 "${A}_{1}(6,-6,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(2,6,-4)$" 13194139534805 true] [17592186311213 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534805 true] [17592186311213 1111 #uuid "a147f309-f3f8-50d0-bd0a-e3cf9539e610" 13194139534805 true] [17592186311214 1034 "${A}_{1}(10,2,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(7,6,-3)$" 13194139534805 true] [17592186311214 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534805 true] [17592186311214 1111 #uuid "bf60c65e-1a30-55f7-9f35-bf29135bc1bf" 13194139534805 true] [17592186311215 1017 #edb/ref 17592186311216 13194139534805 true] [17592186311215 1089 "q-77443" 13194139534805 true] [17592186311215 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534805 true] [17592186311215 1100 "Consider the straight line that passes through $P(1,1,1)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨1,-1,5⟩.$ Find all the possible points $Q$ on that line such that $PQ=3\\sqrt{3}.$" 13194139534805 true] [17592186311215 1113 #uuid "ca1265ac-23c6-5e5b-be9c-b56a47160343" 13194139534805 true] [17592186311215 1145 "First, we find the vector equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-1,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSince $Q$ lies on the line, we know that there must be a real number $t$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OQ} & =⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-1,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-1,5⟩)-⟨1,1,1⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,⟨1,-1,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t,\\,-t,\\,5t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $PQ=3\\sqrt{3},$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PQ & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ |\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ |⟨t,\\,-t,\\,5t⟩| & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{{t}^{2}+(-t)^{2}+(5t)^{2}} & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{27{t}^{2}} & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\pm 3\\sqrt{3}t & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ t & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the values $t=\\pm 1$ into the equation for the line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{O{Q}_{1}}=⟨1,1,1⟩+⟨1,-1,5⟩=⟨2,0,6⟩, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{O{Q}_{2}}=⟨1,1,1⟩-⟨1,-1,5⟩=⟨0,2,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points are ${Q}_{1}(2,0,6)$ and ${Q}_{2}(0,2,-4).$" 13194139534805 true] [17592186311216 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311217 13194139534805 true] [17592186311216 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311218 13194139534805 true] [17592186311216 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311219 13194139534805 true] [17592186311216 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311220 13194139534805 true] [17592186311216 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311221 13194139534805 true] [17592186311216 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534805 true] [17592186311216 1041 "selection" 13194139534805 true] [17592186311216 1104 #edb/ref 17592186311219 13194139534805 true] [17592186311216 1110 #uuid "